# VCART VRHR Aggregator

Reads each of the 16 territories' VCART VRHR files from OneDrive and rolls
them up into one master workbook: `VCART.Region.Nation.Totals.New.xlsx`.

## Files

- **`main.py`** — run this every refresh. Reads the territory files, writes
  `VCART Totals` and `VCART Systems - LIVE`.
- **`summary.py`** — builds the Trends & Takeaways sheet. Called by
  `main.py`; not meant to be run on its own.
- **`config.py`** — territory list, column mappings, header text, colors.
- **`migrate.py`** — one-time tool, only needed if `config.py`'s column
  layout shifts again. Not part of the normal refresh.

## Setup

1. Sync (not download) the **VCART VRHR** subfolder under **ViiV Field
   Reimbursement Managers - 2026** in Teams/SharePoint. `config.py` finds
   it automatically once synced.
2. `python -m venv venv` then `.\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install openpyxl`

If your OneDrive folder isn't found automatically, set `VCART_BASE_DIR` /
`VCART_OUTPUT` as environment variables instead of editing `config.py`.

## Usage

```
python main.py
```

Run monthly, or as often as you want. Safe to run more than once in the
same month — it just refreshes in place instead of duplicating a row.

## What it builds

- **VCART Totals** — territory-level totals: Implementation Barriers,
  Barrier 1/2 tracking, Discovery/Pathway/Tech/Sustainment fields
- **VCART Systems - LIVE** — every real campus row across all 16
  territories
- **Trends & Takeaways** — monthly trend charts, breakdown tables,
  closed-barrier tracking, Days to Close by category

Each sheet keeps a monthly time series (up to 12 months) plus a LIVE
section, and freezes the previous month into a snapshot on rollover
(last 11 kept). The top time-series table's Months/Total Barriers labels
sit at columns D/E, with A–C left blank.

The 4 Barrier 1/2 Start/Close Date columns are hidden by default on both
`VCART Totals` and `VCART Systems - LIVE` (Days to Close stays visible).
Unhide manually in Excel anytime — the next run re-hides them.

## Days to Close & % Campuses Flagged TFRM

NATION's Days to Close is a pooled average of every individual closed
barrier nationwide (Barrier 1 and Barrier 2 tracked separately, scoped to
barriers closed this quarter) — not an average of each territory's own
number. % Campuses Flagged TFRM is a campus-weighted average across
territories, not a plain average. The current month's row in the time
series uses the same calculations as NATION, so they always match.

## If something looks off

- **Blank field with a warning in the console** — the source file's
  column header text changed; add the new wording to the matching list
  in `config.py`.
- **A territory's barrier data is all blank** — that file has no sheet
  matching "barrier movement" yet.
- **Layout looks broken** — delete the output file and let it rebuild
  fresh, or check for a hand-edited date that no longer matches the
  expected format.